  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRCSDK3+UDON-2020.04.03.13.19\n\nIf you tab away from the graph editor or change selection of objects in the hierarchy the graph editor desyncs from the assembly code it is tied to.  At this point any further changes you make to the graph do not result in any functional changes when the world is built and tested.  \n\nDiscovered this with just a simple script where a cube disabled another cube.  After testing the disable functionality I changed the script to be a enable/disable toggle, but the enable functionality never worked.  I destroyed and recreated the component with the full toggle capability from the start and it worked.  Went back and removed the links for the toggle portion and the world continued to have the toggle capability.  Looked at the assembly code and it still listed the full toggle functionality even though the graph no longer had it.\n\nMaking sure to always click the \"Open Udon Graph\" button before making changes seems to work more consistently, but once you get yourself into this state even clicking that doesn't help all the time.\n\n(If the Udon watermark is above the nodes, and you've tried making a change since then, you've gotten yourself into this desync state.)\n\n\n",
